  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Rohingya Refugee Response - Emergency Appeal</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Approximately 670,000 Rohingya Refugees have arrived in Bangladesh since August 2017. They are living in extremely difficult conditions across a number of refugee camps in Cox&apos;s Bazar District. The total population now in need of assistance is 880,000 people. Needs are vast and complex including food, shelter, WASH, health and protection. 

This project is a contribution of &#xa3;10,000 made by ARUP, an international engineering and architectural company, to Caritas Bangladesh&apos;s emergency appeal (EA). In the rapid response phase of the EA, Caritas Bangladesh provided food aid and cooking utensils to 10,000 families. In the revised EA, Caritas Bangladesh will target 30,000 families (approximately 180,000 people) through integrated shelter/WASH/protection services in the line with overall response with other organisations. 

The second approval (October 2018) is a further &#xa3;7,200 donation by ARUP which will be given to Caritas Bangladesh&apos;s emergency appeal which is not fully funded to date.</narrative>
  </description>
